<footer class="provenance">
  <h2>About these tools</h2>

  <p>
    Study aids for <b>ECE/ME 732 — Dynamics of Controlled Systems</b>, built by
    Levi Purdy. <b>Not official course material</b>: not produced, reviewed, or
    endorsed by the instructor or the University. They contain no course
    handouts, lecture material, or homework solutions — only general
    control-systems concepts, written from scratch.
  </p>

  <p>
    <b>Built with AI assistance</b> (Claude), and verified rather than trusted.
    The numerics are checked against known closed-form results before use —
    eigenvalues of known matrices, a rotation correctly reported as a complex
    pair, and the three-mass chain's natural frequencies against
    2·√(k/m)·sin((2j−1)π/14). A browser test suite drives every control and
    asserts the displayed numbers against independently computed values, and a
    second AI model reviews the mathematics for errors.
  </p>

  <p>
    That process has caught real mistakes in these very tools — including a
    claim that a vector on an eigenvector is never rotated, which is false when
    the eigenvalue is negative. <b>If something here disagrees with the lecture,
    the lecture is right.</b> Please tell me if you find an error.
  </p>

  <p class="provenance-links">
    <a href={repo}>Source and verification harness</a>
  </p>
</footer>
